<title>AUSTRALIA: Bank of Queensland half year profit falls.</title>
<headline>Bank of Queensland half year profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to February 28</p>
<p>		  (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     7.995 vs 10.21</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		    12.0   vs 12.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Bank of Queensland Ltd is 45 percent owned by the Queensland Government. The bank also announced a special dividend of 65 cents per share, fully franked.  </p>
<p>    Sales				    52.35 vs 55.38</p>
<p>    Other income			     nil vs  nil</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			     14.0 vs 18.3</p>
<p>    Bad and doubtful debt expense     1.35 vs 1.22</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion)		2.36 vs 2.21</p>
<p>    Net interest income		  41.26 vs 43.52</p>
<p>Pay date May 9</p>
<p>Reg date April 18</p>
<p>    Tax					 4.58 vs 5.72</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    2.38 vs 2.33</p>
<p>    Interest				 58.54 vs 61.38</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
